{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevReflectionTrapezoid","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevReflectionTrapezoid","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevProdEndpoint","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyDerivative"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevErr_add_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevErr_add_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L101-L188","doc":"**`ε_k + ε_{N−1−k}` is exactly the trapezoid remainder on `[θ, θ+h]`.**\n\n    ε_k + ε_{N−1−k} = ½[f(θ) + f(θ+h)] − (1/h)·∫_θ^{θ+h} f,   f = log(2 sin)\n\nwith `θ = kπ/N`, `h = π/N`, so `θ+h = (k+1)π/N` and `1/h = N/π`.  An identity,\nfor every `N` and every `0 < k` with `k+1 < N` — no asymptotics anywhere.\n\nHence the symmetric half of `qou-mlgp` (A)'s error is a trapezoid remainder,\n`O(h²csc²θ)` in the interior, and all of (A)'s remaining difficulty is\nantisymmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevErr","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L97-L99","doc":"The error `ε_k` in the conjectured expansion of `s_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevMainTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevMainTerm","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L92-L95","doc":"The conjectured main term `(N/π)Λ(θ) − ½log(2N sin θ)` of `s_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevLogSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevLogSum","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L88-L90","doc":"`s_k = −∑_{j=1}^{k} log(2 sin(jπ/N))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_two_sin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_two_sin","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L59-L86","doc":"**`∫_a^b log(2 sin t) dt = Λ(a) − Λ(b)`** for `0 < a ≤ b < π`.\n\nThe fundamental theorem of calculus against `hasDerivAt_Lob` (`Λ' = −log(2 sin)`\non `(0, π)`), with the sign flipped out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.Lob_pi_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.Lob_pi_sub","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevReflectionTrapezoid.lean#L52-L57","doc":"**`Λ(π − t) = −Λ(t)`.**  From `Λ(t) = Cl₂(2t)/2`, `2π`-periodicity and\noddness of `Cl₂`: `Cl₂(2π − 2t) = Cl₂(−2t) = −Cl₂(2t)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}